WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.333
The next morning the whole school knew that Sara was in trouble.

2
00:00:06.334 --> 00:00:10.711
Everyone had heard that Miss Minchin wanted to fire Becky.

3
00:00:10.712 --> 00:00:16.054
But it was hard to find a good kitchen maid, so Becky didn't lose her job.

4
00:00:16.055 --> 00:00:19.943
Miss Minchin didn't send Sara away either.

5
00:00:19.944 --> 00:00:24.746
She had practical reasons for wanting to keep Sara at the school.

6
00:00:24.747 --> 00:00:30.484
Sara was teaching some of the other girls, and could perform difficult tasks.

7
00:00:30.485 --> 00:00:34.305
And Miss Minchin didn't have to pay her a cent.

8
00:00:34.306 --> 00:00:41.435
But Sara was given no food that day. As usual she was sent on many errands.

9
00:00:41.436 --> 00:00:45.896
She was even colder and wetter than the day before.

10
00:00:45.897 --> 00:00:52.633
At ten o'clock Sara wearily climbed the steps to the attic.

11
00:00:52.634 --> 00:00:57.636
"Oh, I hope the new things are still there," she whispered.

12
00:00:57.637 --> 00:01:04.368
She opened the door to her room and gasped. The fire was blazing.

13
00:01:04.369 --> 00:01:07.720
Supper for two was waiting on the table.

14
00:01:07.721 --> 00:01:11.460
A number of new things had been brought to the attic.

15
00:01:11.461 --> 00:01:16.196
The ugly mantel was hidden by a rich tapestry.

16
00:01:16.197 --> 00:01:22.338
Colorful fabrics and fans were tacked to the walls, and a long box rested on the floor.

17
00:01:22.339 --> 00:01:26.829
It was covered with a rug and cushions to make a sofa.

18
00:01:26.830 --> 00:01:32.567
"It's like I'm living in a fairy tale!" exclaimed Sara.

19
00:01:32.568 --> 00:01:36.952
She knocked on the wall, and Becky immediately appeared.

20
00:01:36.953 --> 00:01:43.405
"Oh my!" said Becky. Her eyes were wide with amazement.

21
00:01:43.406 --> 00:01:45.932
"Where does it all come from?"

22
00:01:45.933 --> 00:01:49.273
"I have no idea," said Sara.

23
00:01:49.274 --> 00:01:56.024
"But Miss Minchin must never find out what has been happening up here!"

24
00:01:56.025 --> 00:02:01.153
Sara discovered that she had a new mattress and pillows.

25
00:02:01.154 --> 00:02:05.087
Her old mattress and pillow were now on Becky's bed.

26
00:02:05.088 --> 00:02:08.309
So Becky’s bed was now softer too.

27
00:02:08.310 --> 00:02:12.814
From that day on, life became more wonderful.

28
00:02:12.815 --> 00:02:16.753
Every night there was something new in Sara's room.

29
00:02:16.754 --> 00:02:22.286
Pictures covered the ugly walls. New pieces of furniture appeared.

30
00:02:22.287 --> 00:02:26.370
A bookshelf was filled with books.

31
00:02:26.371 --> 00:02:29.674
Miss Minchin was as harsh as ever.

32
00:02:29.675 --> 00:02:34.028
The cook and other servants were still rude to Sara.

33
00:02:34.029 --> 00:02:38.196
She was never allowed to speak to Ermengarde and Lottie.

34
00:02:38.197 --> 00:02:41.368
Lavinia continued to sneer at her.

35
00:02:41.369 --> 00:02:47.460
But Sara didn't mind. She had her lovely room to look forward to all day.

36
00:02:47.461 --> 00:02:53.149
She also had a hot meal every evening.

37
00:02:53.150 --> 00:02:58.284
And Sara enjoyed having a special secret to keep from Miss Minchin.

38
00:02:58.285 --> 00:03:03.558
"If you only knew!" she thought whenever Miss Minchin scolded

39
00:03:03.559 --> 00:03:09.778
her. But Miss Minchin had noticed something different about

40
00:03:09.779 --> 00:03:16.066
Sara. "Sara is looking remarkably well," Miss Minchin said to her sister one

41
00:03:16.067 --> 00:03:22.015
afternoon. "Yes, she used to look so starved," Miss Amelia

42
00:03:22.016 --> 00:03:26.077
replied. "Why do you say that?" snapped the

43
00:03:26.078 --> 00:03:28.874
headmistress. "She always had enough to

44
00:03:28.875 --> 00:03:34.980
eat." "Of course," Miss Amelia quickly agreed. She hated upsetting her

45
00:03:34.981 --> 00:03:40.427
sister. "There's something defiant about Sara," Miss Minchin went

46
00:03:40.428 --> 00:03:47.942
on."She's still acting like she's a princess. I find that most annoying."

47
00:03:47.943 --> 00:03:54.126
One day a deliveryman came to the school. Sara was sent to open the door.

48
00:03:54.127 --> 00:03:57.817
The man handed her several packages.

49
00:03:57.818 --> 00:04:03.803
They were all addressed to "The Little Girl in the Right-hand Room in the Attic."

50
00:04:03.804 --> 00:04:09.327
Miss Minchin came downstairs as Sara was staring at the address labels.

51
00:04:09.328 --> 00:04:14.722
"Take those to the young lady to whom they belong," said the headmistress.

52
00:04:14.723 --> 00:04:17.823
"Don't just stand there staring at them."

53
00:04:17.824 --> 00:04:23.285
"But they're addressed to me," said Sara quietly.

54
00:04:23.286 --> 00:04:29.769
"To you?" exclaimed Miss Minchin. "Well then, open them right now!"

55
00:04:29.770 --> 00:04:34.524
"I don't know where they came from," Sara said.

56
00:04:34.525 --> 00:04:44.180
She opened the packages and found all kinds of beautiful, warm clothing—shoes, stockings, gloves, and a nice hat.

57
00:04:44.181 --> 00:04:48.441
There was even an umbrella and a winter coat.

58
00:04:48.442 --> 00:04:50.360
Pinned to the coat was a note:

59
00:04:50.361 --> 00:04:56.086
To be worn every day. Will be replaced when necessary.

60
00:04:56.087 --> 00:05:00.069
Miss Minchin was quite upset when she saw the clothing.

61
00:05:00.070 --> 00:05:03.240
Did Sara have a relative looking out for her?

62
00:05:03.241 --> 00:05:07.215
What if this person discovered how poorly Sara had been treated?

63
00:05:07.216 --> 00:05:10.121
He would be angry with Miss Minchin.

64
00:05:10.122 --> 00:05:15.747
"Well," she said in a voice that was softer than her usual one with Sara.

65
00:05:15.748 --> 00:05:19.064
"Someone has been very kind to you.

66
00:05:19.065 --> 00:05:22.385
You might as well change into your new clothes.

67
00:05:22.386 --> 00:05:27.916
After you are dressed, you may come downstairs and learn your lessons in the schoolroom.

68
00:05:27.917 --> 00:05:32.502
There's no need to do any more errands today."

69
00:05:32.503 --> 00:05:39.281
When Sara entered the schoolroom thirty minutes later, the girls whispered and stared.

70
00:05:39.282 --> 00:05:44.900
Sara was dressed in a beautiful dress and she wore a ribbon in her hair.

71
00:05:44.901 --> 00:05:48.344
She looked just like the old Sara.

72
00:05:48.345 --> 00:05:54.316
Jessie elbowed Lavinia. "Look at Princess Sara!"

73
00:05:54.317 --> 00:05:58.670
"Come sit here by me, Sara," Miss Minchin said.

74
00:05:58.671 --> 00:06:02.502
Sara went to her old seat of honor and sat down.

75
00:06:02.503 --> 00:06:10.588
Then she opened a book and began to study.

